		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4853&amp;p=35709#p35709"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Thanks for a another great feature in this firmware, i installed this on my UV390 and my 3 MD9600, works great. One of my 9600 does not have a GPS, it was a bit to fiddle around to find the correct setting to use for a fixed poisition between the setting in the Options- APRS, CPS and the location used for the satelite tracking, i have it working now...<br>I wonder if there is a way to use different power levels for the channel i'm working in (100mW to the Openspot) and the APRS beacon. Ideal would be something like channel per CPS for that Channel and the APRS beacon power comes from the master power level or is set in the CPS - APRS menu next to the frequency for the beacon.  <br><br>thanks and 73</div></blockquote>I agree that beaconing at 50mW/100mW isn't that great...<br>Hence, I will add a power level in the APRS settings (firmware side), defaulted to "master" or 1W power setting (IDK right now).<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Wed Feb 12, 2025 6:05 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
